# Evaluation fixture, not a real ownership map. Inert in the skills repository, where
# GitHub reads CODEOWNERS only at the repository root, .github/ or docs/. It takes
# effect once the fixture is copied to the root of a disposable repository.
#
# Owners use the reserved example.com domain, so no real account is ever requested.
# Replace them with a second account you control when a trial needs a real
# code-owner review request.
#
# app.py and test_app.py are unowned on purpose, so ordinary changes can be `agent`.

/.github/     fixture-maintainer@example.com
/AGENTS.md    fixture-maintainer@example.com
/CODEOWNERS   fixture-maintainer@example.com
